<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP SECOND ROUND, SECOND LEG RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP SECOND ROUND, SECOND LEG RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of South American</p>
<p>Libertadores Cup second round, second leg matches:</p>
<p>Played on Wednesday</p>
<p>In Santiago:</p>
<p>Colo Colo (Chile) 1 Nacional (Uruguay) 2 (halftime 0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Colo Colo - Fernando Vergara (55)</p>
<p>Nacional - Fernando Kanapkis (45), Mario Barilko (48)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Colo Colo won 4-3 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Santa Cruz, Bolivia:</p>
<p>Oriente Petrolero (Bolivia) 1 Universidad Catolica (Chile) 5</p>
<p>(0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Oriente Petrolero: Raul Medeiros (90)</p>
<p>Universidad Catolica - David Bisconti (3, 43 and 56),</p>
<p>Ricardo Lunari (72), Cate (78)</p>
<p>Attendance - 12,000</p>
<p>Universidad Catlica win 9-1 on aggregate</p>
<p>In Belo Horizonte, Brazil:</p>
<p>Cruzeiro (Brazil) 2 Nacional (Ecuador) 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Cruzeiro - Marcelo (62, 69)</p>
<p>Nacional - Jofre Arroyo (90)</p>
<p>Attendance: 24,000.</p>
<p>Aggregate score 2-2. Cruzeiro won 5-3 on penalties.</p>
<p>Already qualified for quarter-finals: Bolivar (Bolivia),</p>
<p>Gremio (Brazil), Penarol (Uruguay), Racing Club (Argentina),</p>
<p>Sporting Cristal (Peru).</p>
</text>
